Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.21,0:00:01.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two crashes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.60,0:00:02.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,One death.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.48,0:00:04.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,And Senna still got in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.29,0:00:10.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is his story, from a go kart in\NSão Paulo to a courtroom in Rome.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.83,0:00:21.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,Ayrton Senna was a\NBrazilian racing driver
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.42,0:00:24.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,and a three time Formula\NOne world champion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.35,0:00:30.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,He was born in São\NPaulo on 21 March 1960,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.56,0:00:32.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,and began racing karts at thirteen,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.52,0:00:35.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,in a kart his father built\Naround a lawnmower engine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.13,0:00:41.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,He won the South American\NKart Championship in 1977,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.00,0:00:44.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,and twice finished runner up\Nat the world championship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.81,0:00:50.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 1981 he moved to England\Nfor single seater racing,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.38,0:00:53.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,and in 1983 he won the\NBritish Formula Three title,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.69,0:00:55.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,after a close fight with Martin Brundle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.89,0:01:02.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,He made his Formula One debut in\N1984, with the small Toleman team.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.89,0:01:07.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,At Monaco that year, in heavy rain,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.48,0:01:10.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,he started thirteenth\Nand finished second,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.02,0:01:13.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,closing fast on the leader Alain\NProst when the race was stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.87,0:01:19.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,In April 1985, driving for Lotus,\Nhe won his first Grand Prix,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:21.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,in the wet at Estoril, in Portugal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.37,0:01:27.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 1986, on a Brazilian\Ntelevision programme,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.82,0:01:29.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,he explained why he raced.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.81,0:01:43.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 1988 he joined McLaren,\Nalongside Alain Prost.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.12,0:01:47.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,The two won fifteen of the\Nsixteen races that season,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.33,0:01:49.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,and Senna took his first world title.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.35,0:01:54.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,He won at Monaco six times,\Nmore than any other driver.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.81,0:01:58.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,His rivalry with Prost was fierce.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.40,0:02:03.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,At Suzuka in 1989, and again in 1990,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.24,0:02:06.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,the two collided, and each time\Nit settled the championship.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.65,0:02:13.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,He won the world title\Nin 1988, 1990 and 1991.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.84,0:02:17.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,By 1994 he had won forty\None Grand Prix races
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.51,0:02:19.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,and taken sixty five pole positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.05,0:02:24.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the rain at Donington in 1993,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.70,0:02:29.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,he passed four drivers on the first lap\Nto take the lead, and went on to win.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.87,0:02:36.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 28 March 1993, he won the\NBrazilian Grand Prix at Interlagos,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.83,0:02:38.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,in front of his home crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.05,0:02:44.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,When the race ended, Brazilian\Nfans ran onto the track to celebrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.09,0:02:49.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,For 1994, he left McLaren\Nfor a new team, Williams.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.03,0:02:53.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,But the season started badly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.13,0:02:57.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,He took pole position in\Nboth of the first two races,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.54,0:03:01.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,and finished neither, so after\Ntwo races he had no points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.65,0:03:09.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,The weekend began\Non Friday, 29 April.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.47,0:03:14.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,The young Brazilian driver\NRubens Barrichello lost control
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.72,0:03:17.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,of his Jordan on a kerb\Nand hit a safety fence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.83,0:03:22.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,He survived, with a\Nbroken nose and arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.46,0:03:26.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,after the circuit's chief doctor, Sid\NWatkins, reached him quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.47,0:03:30.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,Senna went straight to\Ncheck on his compatriot.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.85,0:03:36.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then Senna went back to his car, and\Nset the fastest time in qualifying.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.29,0:03:41.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,On Saturday, 30 April,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.58,0:03:45.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,the Austrian driver Roland\NRatzenberger crashed in qualifying,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.06,0:03:45.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,and died.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.53,0:03:48.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,He drove for the small team Simtek.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.79,0:03:54.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,Qualifying was stopped for almost\Nfifty minutes, and when it resumed,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.80,0:03:58.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,several teams, including Senna's\NWilliams, took no further part.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.55,0:04:04.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was the first death at a Formula\NOne race weekend since 1982.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.09,0:04:10.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,Watkins later wrote that he urged\NSenna to give up racing altogether.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.87,0:04:14.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,Watkins wrote that Senna answered
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.64,0:04:16.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,that some things are\Nout of our control,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.32,0:04:18.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,and that he could not quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.17,0:04:23.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,On Sunday morning, he filmed an\Nin car lap for French television,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.10,0:04:26.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,where his old rival Alain\NProst was working.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.18,0:04:30.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,He greeted Prost on camera,\Nand Prost said he was surprised.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.69,0:04:35.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Senna started Sunday's\Nrace from pole position.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.77,0:04:43.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,On Sunday, 1 May 1994, an accident at\Nthe start brought out the safety car.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.51,0:04:48.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Racing resumed on lap\Nsix, with Senna leading.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.71,0:04:54.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,On lap seven, his Williams left the\Ntrack at the Tamburello corner,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.29,0:04:55.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the race was stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.51,0:04:59.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,This video does not show the accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.73,0:05:03.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,Ayrton Senna died that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.26,0:05:04.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,He was thirty four.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.55,0:05:10.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,Sources disagree on the exact time\Nof death, so we do not give one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.51,0:05:15.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,The race was restarted, and\NMichael Schumacher won it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.01,0:05:26.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,His body was flown home, and on 5\NMay, São Paulo held his state funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.53,0:05:30.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,Brazil declared days\Nof national mourning,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.02,0:05:33.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the coffin crossed\Nthe city on a fire engine,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.69,0:05:35.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,draped in the Brazilian flag.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.45,0:05:40.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,More than two hundred thousand\Npeople visited him as he lay in state,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.24,0:05:43.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,and estimates of the\Ncrowd at the funeral run
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.48,0:05:45.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,from one million to\Nabout three million.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.95,0:05:51.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,Rivals carried his coffin,\Namong them Alain Prost,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.30,0:05:53.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,Gerhard Berger and\NRubens Barrichello.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.97,0:05:58.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Tamburello corner\Nwas rebuilt as a chicane,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.08,0:06:01.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the drivers safety\Ngroup was re-established.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.65,0:06:09.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,In November 1994, his family\Nfounded the Instituto Ayrton Senna,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.04,0:06:11.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,led by his sister Viviane.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.18,0:06:15.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,It works on education for children and\Nteenagers from low income families.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.63,0:06:22.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,Italian prosecutors investigated,\Nand a judicial report in 1995 pointed
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.96,0:06:25.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,at a steering column failure\Nafter a pre-race adjustment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.03,0:06:31.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,A trial opened at Imola\Nin February 1997.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.78,0:06:33.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,Six men were charged\Nwith manslaughter:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.74,0:06:35.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,the Williams team\Nowner Frank Williams,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.72,0:06:37.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,technical director Patrick Head,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.47,0:06:40.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,designer Adrian Newey,\Nand three race organisers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.55,0:06:44.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,The case centred on\Nthe steering column,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.52,0:06:46.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,which had been lengthened\Nat Senna's request.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.89,0:06:52.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 16 December 1997,\Nall six were acquitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.99,0:06:56.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,In January 2003,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.28,0:07:00.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,Italy's Supreme Court of Cassation\Noverturned the acquittals
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.74,0:07:02.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,of Head and Newey and\Nordered a new appeal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.25,0:07:10.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,In May 2005, the new appeal\Ncourt found Newey not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.15,0:07:14.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,Head appealed again,\Nto be fully cleared.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.18,0:07:18.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,In April 2007, the Supreme\NCourt rejected that appeal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.21,0:07:21.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,Reports
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.67,0:07:25.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,of the ruling say the court found the\Nsteering modification poorly designed
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.98,0:07:27.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,and poorly executed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.70,0:07:30.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,and that a steering column\Nfailure caused the accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.80,0:07:34.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,It held Head responsible for a failure\Nof control, but too late to punish.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.93,0:07:40.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,Williams has always argued that\Nthe column broke only on impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.36,0:07:43.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,Head himself believed that\NSenna had made a driving error.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.97,0:07:49.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,So after nearly thirteen years,\Nthe courts named a cause,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.42,0:07:51.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the team still disputes it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.25,0:07:56.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,The highest court said a\Nsteering column failed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.44,0:07:59.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,but the team says it\Nbroke only on impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.35,0:08:02.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,After nearly thirteen years of trials,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.82,0:08:05.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,who gets to say what really\Nhappened at Tamburello?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.56,0:01:36.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the end, it is a pleasure: something good that brings positive energy. (our translation)
